        "binding_energy_per_nucleon_mev": null,
        "narrative": "Radium-223 (223Ra, Ra-223) is an alpha-emitting isotope of radium with half-life 11.435 days. It was discovered in 1905 by T. Godlewski, a Polish chemist from Krak\u00f3w, and was historically known as actinium X (AcX). Radium-223 dichloride is an alpha particle-emitting radiotherapy drug that mimics calcium and forms complexes with hydroxyapatite at areas of increased bone turnover. The principal use of radium-223, as a radiopharmaceutical to treat metastatic cancers in bone, takes advantage of its chemical similarity to calcium, and the short range of the alpha radiation it emits.",
